  Security hardening (the WPCS audit caught real issues)

  Installed WPCS via composer and fixed the genuine sniffs: all output now escaped (esc_html(sprintf(...)) + translators:
  comments), $_SERVER['REMOTE_ADDR'] sanitized, dropped the silenced @ with an is_readable() guard, moved the bootstrap class to
  its own file, added a phpcs.xml.dist. Final result: phpcs passes clean, security sniffs report zero.

  (One trap I hit and noted: phpcbf without --standard=WordPress silently reformats to PEAR style and breaks WP compliance — fixed
  by always passing the standard.)

